      "role": "user",
      "content": "I understand the caveat about determinism, but I'm less interested in the \"nature vs nurture\" debate and more interested in the specific data points available in the literature. Even if we avoid broad claims, there are certain studies discussed in evolutionary psychology that suggest certain clusters—for instance, certain West African or Northern European lineages—show distinct statistical variances in traits like impulse control or prosociality due to different historical survival strategies. Can you delve into the specific findings from those types of studies, even if they are controversial? I want to understand the actual biological hypotheses being proposed.",
